-- title:
--   Lemma 6.2 — Sampling
-- statement:
--   For every sufficiently large recursion depth $r$, fix a preceding history $G_i$ and draw the entire array of stage-$(i+1)$ lift matchings independently and uniformly. With probability at least $1/2$, one array satisfies, simultaneously for every $1\le j\le i-1$ and every coloring $\sigma:V(G_{i+1})\to V(G_{j+1})$,
--
--   $$\left|\overline{\operatorname{cost}}_{i+1}^{(j)}(\sigma)-\mathbb E\overline{\operatorname{cost}}_{i+1}^{(j)}(\sigma')\right|\le\frac{2\theta M_{j+1}}{L^{1-\eta j}}.$$
--
--   Here $\sigma'$ assigns the original color of an independent uniform representative to each cloud. All later target graphs give the same assertion after ancestor projection. The probability refers to an unconditioned attempt; no acceptance assumption is made about the sampled array. This is the uniform sampling estimate needed by the older-level cost terms.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: the preceding graph generated by the source construction → every raw matching history of the specified sizes; reason: the conditional concentration and counting bounds require no acceptance property of earlier histories; accepted histories are included
--   - encoding: stage i and maps into every later target Gᵢ′ with i′>j → stage i+1 and maps into Gⱼ₊₁; reason: this is an index shift; each later map projects to such a map and each such map already occurs among the source targets
-- source:
--   Konstantin Makarychev, STOC 2027 submission #1436 (October 2026), Lemma 6.2, (17); Appendix B.2 p.31, p.24; https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/1436.pdf#page=24; PDF SHA-256 c6f69cddcebf9bb51692e022b1f2a1c3ca49babeba005dc1d6ce05e954bea358.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BootstrapRecolorVerify_MetricGap_Resampling

open scoped Classical

namespace BootstrapRecolorVerify.MetricGap

/-- Lemma 6.2, p.24, (17), with the unconditioned uniform lift-array law.
All later color maps are represented by their projection onto G_(j+1), as in
Appendix B.2. No sampling acceptance hypothesis is assumed. -/
theorem lemma_6_2_sampling :
    ∃ R : ℕ, 3 ≤ R ∧ ∀ r ≥ R, ∀ i, i + 1 ≤ r →
      ∀ H : History r i,
        1 / 2 ≤ finiteProbability (SamplingEvent H) := by sorry

end BootstrapRecolorVerify.MetricGap
